2 264 1121","wp":"ja:広島市現代美術館","wifi":1,"ds":"The Hiroshima City Museum of Contemporary Art (広島市現代美術館, Hiroshima-shi Gendai Bijutsukan) is an art museum founded in 1989. It is in Hijiyama Park in Hiroshima, Japan. The building was designed by architect Kisho Kurokawa.","wpu":"Hiroshima City Museum of Contemporary Art","img":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/d/df/Hiroshima_City_Museum_of_Contemporary_Art_01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled"},{"n":"白神社の岩礁","g":"sights","k":"attraction","la":34.390404,"lo":132.45625,"d":4205},{"n":"Donkey Hotel","g":"sights","k":"attraction","la":34.391362,"lo":132.462639,"d":4265},{"n":"Rai Sanyo Shiseki Museum","g":"sights","k":"museum","la":34.391382,"lo":132.457244,"d":4300,"w":"http://raisanyou.com","wp":"ja:頼山陽史跡資料館"},{"n":"旧日本銀行広島支店資料室","g":"sights","k":"museum","la":34.391379,"lo":132.456729,"d":4306},{"n":"Fukuromachi Elementary School Peace Museum","g":"sights","k":"museum","la":34.391546,"lo":132.458252,"d":4308,"wp":"en:Fukuromachi Elementary School Peace Museum","ds":"The Fukuromachi Elementary School Peace Museum (袋町小学校平和資料館, Fukuromachi Shogakkou Heiwa Shiryokan) is a peace museum in Fukuromachi, Naka-ku, Hiroshima, Japan. The school was one of the closest schools to ground zero when the atomic bomb fell on August 6, 1945. They lost about 160 students and teachers and the building was heavily damaged.","wpu":"Fukuromachi Elementary School Peace Museum","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ce/Fukuromachi_Elementary_School_Peace_Museum01.JPG/960px-Fukuromachi_Elementary_School_Peace_Museum01.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Former Hiroshima Branch of the Bank of Japan","g":"sights","k":"gallery","la":34.391467,"lo":132.456816,"d":4314,"h":"10:00-17:00","wp":"ja:旧日本銀行広島支店"},{"n":"Hiroshima Peace Memorial Museum East Building","g":"sights","k":"museum","la":34.391548,"lo":132.453098,"d":4381,"h":